Qwen2.5 tool calling done client-side for local Ollama runs.

Why: Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint (seen on 0.33.1) mishandles tools for
Qwen2.5 in two ways:
  1. Its tool-call parser silently drops any call to a tool that isn't in the
     request's tool list. The reply comes back with no text and no tool calls,
     and tau2 aborts the whole task ("AssistantMessage/UserMessage must have
     either content or tool_calls"). In telecom the agent and user have
     different tools, so this crashed 21-43% of telecom tasks. Retries can't
     help: with a fixed seed they replay the same conversation.
  2. It renders tool schemas into the prompt as Go struct dumps
     ({get_customer_by_phone Finds a ... {object <nil> <nil> [...] {...}}})
     instead of JSON.

What: when TAU2_QWEN_TOOLS_IN_PROMPT=1 (set by scripts/run_tau2.py for
qwen2.5* models), generate() writes tools, tool calls and tool results as plain
chat text exactly as Qwen2.5's official chat template renders them (checked
character-for-character against the Hugging Face template), sends no `tools`
field, and parses <tool_call> blocks out of the reply itself. A call to a tool
the caller doesn't have now reaches tau2, which answers with its normal
"Tool '...' not found." error and the conversation continues, as it would with
a hosted API. A reply whose <tool_call> block isn't valid JSON is kept as plain
text (as vLLM's hermes parser does) instead of crashing on json.loads.

